report.append("\nEach source CSV record is 155 bytes including its terminating LF. Each per-case header-plus-record block is 179 bytes. Their exact hashes appear in the addendum and `records.json`. The ordered four-unit header-plus-records selection is 644 bytes, SHA-256 `f34c87e11bc77f02997f41aaae17cf6958ce02976b9621886d96c03029b27af0`, matching the previously recorded sample hash (`run10_harness3/REPORT.md:72`, `run10_review3/REPORT.md:147`). The preserved run10 subset list at `run10/agent/results/reproduce/units-check/files/results/frodock_setup.csv:1–5` supplies another retained copy.\n")
report.append("The canonical source-file names are copied from the earlier index-derived CSV rows cited above. Their remote index source is the pinned `index.parquet`, with exact row selection by full `id` and canonical `apo_R_pdb`/`apo_L_pdb` fields. The PINDER archive’s `src/pinder-methods/pinder/methods/preprocess/__init__.py:30–55` reads `apo_receptor` and `apo_ligand` and writes the two prepared files; `src/pinder-core/pinder/core/index/system.py:198–240,767–790` loads those canonical monomer paths and assigns R/L chain labels. The preparation route does not call the separate native-alignment helpers. Run9’s setup command and manifest assembly are recorded in `run9/agent/harness/setup.sh:3975–4005`, with observed rows in saved `out/setup/setup.log:205,207,211,217`. No prepared remote structural tree was retained for independent new byte hashing; the exact copied artifacts here are prepared CSV records, plus the recorded canonical source pins and existing preparation route. Raw-source hashes are not represented as hashes of serialized prepared PDBs.\n")
